[{"sha":"29c53517cf8e316f02ecadf525b142c15f8eb386","node_id":"C_kwDOFcwZ1doAKDI5YzUzNTE3Y2Y4ZTMxNmYwMmVjYWRmNTI1YjE0MmMxNWY4ZWIzODY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Thomas R. Murrills","email":"68410468+thorimur@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-10-09T06:00:43Z"},"committer":{"name":"Thomas R. Murrills","email":"68410468+thorimur@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-10-09T06:00:43Z"},"message":"chore: format imports (#44513)\n\nThis PR formats imports throughout Mathlib by grouping imports into visibility blocks separated by a newline (`public import`/`import`/`import all`), then sorting within each block by `meta`/(non-meta), and then sorting alphabetically. This uses `scripts/runSkimmer.sh` to apply the suggestions generated in #44507. (Files outside of `Mathlib/` are not touched.)\r\n\r\nThis was discussed among reviewers in the mathlib reviewers channel on Zulip in the topic \"linting imports\", as well as incidentally in the latter part of [this topic](https://leanprover.zulipchat.com/#narrow/channel/144837-PR-reviews/topic/chore.3A.20demote.20public.20imports.20.2343918/with/625621866).\r\n\r\n(Note: this does not format Mathlib.Tactic.Common yet, since that file makes deliberate choices about import ordering.)\r\n\r\n(Note for regeneration purposes: this technically used a transient skimmer lakefile dependency and `lake build Mathlib:applyCurrentTryThis` instead of the script per se, due to the header linter's sensitivity to the package directory and implementation details of the `runSkimmer` script. This may be fixed in the future.)\n\nCo-authored-by: Kim Morrison <kim@tqft.net>","tree":{"sha":"95893be144d7b8354c71c8914a29b28f079bc4fa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leanprover-community/mathlib4/git/trees/95893be144d7b8354c71c8914a29b28f079bc4fa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/leanprover-community/mathlib4/git/commits/29c53517cf8e316f02ecadf525b142c15f8eb386","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":nul